implementationPlan.description:
Modify the message callback in nats.go (lines 148-169) to distinguish unmarshal errors from handler errors. Change the unmarshal error path from ACK to NAK with delay:

```go
cb := func(msg *nats.Msg) {
    var packet pb.BusPacket
    if err := proto.Unmarshal(msg.Data, &packet); err != nil {
        log.Printf("nats bus: poison pill - failed to unmarshal packet: %v", err)
        // NAK with delay instead of ACK — gives NATS a chance to redeliver
        // After max redeliveries (configured on the consumer), NATS moves to DLQ
        if nakErr := msg.NakWithDelay(5 * time.Second); nakErr != nil {
            log.Printf("nats bus: failed to NAK poison pill: %v", nakErr)
        }
        return
    }
    // ... rest of handler unchanged
}
```

This ensures unparseable messages are retried (with backoff) instead of silently lost. NATS JetStream consumers have a MaxDeliver setting that moves messages to the dead letter queue after N attempts.
